  "notes": "Modified cash basis city (recorded as basis cash). Trimmed PDF 8 pages: p1 net position (government-wide, modified cash), p2 activities, p3 governmental funds balance sheet, p4 governmental funds receipts/disbursements/fund balances (Total Governmental Funds column), p5 enterprise net position, p6 enterprise revenues/expenses/net position, p7 enterprise cash flows, p8 budget schedule. Governmental roll: 2,237,278 + 2,081,574 - 1,850,548 - 26,332 = 2,441,972. Governmental interfund transfers net to zero in the total column (shown as -), so transfers_in/out null. Governmental ending cash includes certificates of deposit 499,331 (shown as ending_investments for information, not added). Taxes line not split because p2 general receipts tax lines (1,029,125) do not equal p4 Taxes (1,013,657). Business-type: enterprise statements (p5-p7) are accrual style; business_type beginning/ending net position (3,383,819 / 2,976,541) come from p6 and differ from government-wide modified cash net position on p1 (2,444,784 beginning / 2,035,886 ending; p5 reconciliation shows 2,035,886). Business-type receipts = operating revenues + nonoperating investment earnings; disbursements = operating expenses + interest expense; capital contributions (net) 27,625 in business_type.other_financing; roll: 3,383,819 + 2,436,430 - 2,871,333 + 27,625 = 2,976,541. Proprietary cash-flow block left null (cash basis entity). Balance sheet uses p1 total column (no liabilities on modified cash basis). Detail: p8 budget schedule only lists per-fund actual totals (no budget by line, no itemization, includes beginning balance and transfers/contributions that duplicate p4 and p6), so detail left empty. Read pages 1-8 of 8.",
